{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "id": "08-module-scope-reference",
  "title": "Module-scope reference: handle(...) and Repo#Seed are referenced at package scope",
  "rule_pack": "rules-static-v1",
  "provenance": {
    "kind": "synthetic",
    "source": "hand-authored adversarial static case",
    "seeded_fault": null
  },
  "context": {
    "index": "97eef94d35edf8b9843068aeca622667130796f43989dcc8af4ac6dc50e26041"
  },
  "review_notes": [
    "`handle(\"GET /jobs/{id}\", GetJob)` runs at package scope, so its references to GetJob and to Repo#Seed have no enclosing symbol: scip_module_scope_reference rows, no scip_may_reference.",
    "route -> handler is supported: static_route_handler needs route_handler_location, the definition site and the callable symbol, not a call edge.",
    "`init reaches storage` is unresolved: static_reaches needs a root symbol and a call edge, and a module-scope reference has neither."
  ],
